course: dictionary
lesson: 1213
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. Look at the words around the word and ask, what would make sense here? «Peeking under the blindfold in blind man's buff is soon seen, and then the others won't let you be "it" any more.» A blindfold and "it" tell you that buff is the name of a game, not a word for polishing.
explain: The same word can change meaning in a new sentence. Buff can mean to polish something until it shines, or it can mean a fan who knows a lot about one subject. «She's a history buff» means she loves history and knows lots about it. Read the whole sentence before you decide.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense. If you think buff means polish, does «He's a history polish» work? It does not, so buff must mean something else here. When the clues are still not clear, use a dictionary.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: One word can have several meanings, so always check the clues.
fact: «Buff» can mean to polish something by rubbing it with a soft cloth until it shines.
fact: A «buff» is a person who knows and loves a lot about one subject, such as a «film buff».
fact: «Buff» can also be a pale yellow-brown colour, like light leather, and «buff up» means to build strong muscles.
exercise: Sam is told to «buff the shoes until they shine». What does buff mean here? | *To polish by rubbing with a soft cloth | To throw them away | Cover in mud | To paint them black
exercise: Ella says, «She's a history buff.» What does buff mean in this sentence? | A kind of sports shoe | A pale yellow-brown colour | Something that is very old | *Someone who knows and loves a lot about history
exercise: Find and copy the word in «Peeking under the blindfold in blind man's buff is soon seen» that names a game. | *buff | seen | blindfold | peeking
test: Jamie wants to buff up for football, so he does press-ups every day. What does buff up mean? | To wash the car | To fall asleep early | To read more books | *To build strong muscles
test: In a video game, a sword gets buffed. What does buff mean here? | It turns pale yellow | It breaks into pieces | It is lost in the forest | *It becomes stronger
exam: Which meaning of buff is a pale yellow-brown colour, like light leather? | Ancient | Sparkling | Bright red | *Buff
